    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> be three events having probabilities&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math><br />For any event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></math> denotes its complement, then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?"
